# What the image build does not need.
#
# The context is the repo root and there was no .dockerignore, so every build
# uploaded ~500 MB of .git, node_modules and local worktrees to the daemon.
# Size is the small problem. The real one is that `COPY frontend .` in
# backend/Dockerfile runs AFTER `npm ci`, so the host's node_modules landed on
# top of the one the container had just installed — darwin-arm64 binaries
# inside a linux image. It worked only because COPY merges rather than
# replaces, leaving the linux binary present to win. That is luck, and the kind
# that runs out on a dependency bump with an unreadable error.

# Version control. Also keeps repository history out of every build stage.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Installed and built artifacts: the container builds its own.
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
backend/internal/ui/dist

# Local tooling, worktrees and drafts. .claude alone is ~200 MB here.
.claude
.claire
.security
.remember
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Not part of any image.
docker
docs

# Test output. Globbed, because these land in backend/ — a pattern without a
# slash matches at the root only, which is the same reason *.md is not here.
**/coverage.out
**/*.test
